How to generate analyzer: 

   1. cd Gen++

   2. source env

   3. ksh

   4. SELECT ONE
      mk myquery/compound-c   (for non-decomposed ++ )
      OR 
      mk myquery/compound-d   (for decomposed ++ )  

      A file called "analyzer" is generated at directory Gen++

   5. mv analyzer cfront

How to analyze a C program "file.C":

   1. go to the corresponding directory such as Gen++/SteveCode

   2. CC file.C

   Two files are generated for file.C: fileC.component and
                                       fileC.control 


     
 
